{"name":"Healing Retreat","hex":"#bac2aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"healing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process where the cells in the body regenerate and repair themselves.","An act of healing, as by a faith healer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of heal"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/healing"},{"term":"retreat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of pulling back or withdrawing, as from something dangerous, or unpleasant.\n\nThe act of reversing direction and receding from a forward position.\n Withdrawal by a military force from a dangerous position or from enemy attack.","The act of reversing direction and receding from a forward position."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To withdraw from a position, go back.\n To withdraw military forces.","To withdraw military forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/retreat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Healing","blocks":[{"text":"Regarding physical trauma or disease suffered by an organism, healing involves the repairing of damaged tissue(s), organs and the biological system as a whole and resumption of (normal) functioning. Medicine includes the process by which the cells in the body regenerate and repair to reduce the size of a damaged or necrotic area and replace it with new living tissue. The replacement can happen in two ways: by regeneration in which the necrotic cells are replaced by new cells that form \"like\" tissue as was originally there; or by repair in which injured tissue is replaced with scar tissue. Most organs will heal using a mixture of both mechanisms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/417_Tissue_Repair.jpg/330px-417_Tissue_Repair.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Healing","wikidata":"Q1581290"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/1280px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg/500px-Haavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_%2826901645371%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wounded patients at the Red Cross Hospital in Tampere, Finland during the 1918 Finnish Civil War","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaavoittuneita_Punaisen_ristin_sairaalassa_Tampereella_(26901645371).jpg"}],"sounds":{"healing":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/En-us-healing.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cf/En-us-healing.ogg/En-us-healing.ogg.mp3"}],"retreat":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/En-us-retreat.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5a/En-us-retreat.ogg/En-us-retreat.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-retreat.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.